-- title:
--   Reducedness of κ(A)⊗_A R versus R/mathfrak m_A R
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative local ring, with $\mathrm{maximalIdeal}\,A = \mathfrak m_A$ and residue field $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A = A/\mathfrak m_A$, and let $R$ be a commutative ring equipped with an $A$-algebra structure; no finiteness, Noetherian or flatness hypothesis is imposed, and $R$ is not assumed local. The assertion is an equivalence of two reducedness statements: the ring $(A/\mathfrak m_A)\otimes_A R$, the base change of $R$ along the residue map of $A$, is reduced (that is, it has no nonzero nilpotent elements) if and only if the quotient ring $R/\mathfrak m_A R$ is reduced, where $\mathfrak m_A R$ denotes the image ideal $(\mathrm{maximalIdeal}\,A).\mathrm{map}\,(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,A\,R)$, i.e. the ideal of $R$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_A$ under the structure map $A \to R$. Both sides are the statement that the special fibre of $R$ over $A$ is reduced, in its tensor-product and its quotient presentation respectively.
--
--   This is the standard identification $(A/\mathfrak a)\otimes_A M \cong M/\mathfrak a M$ in the case $\mathfrak a = \mathfrak m_A$ and $M = R$ an algebra, used to pass freely between the two presentations of the special fibre. It is invoked in the verification that certain special fibres of quotients of adic completions arising in the study of modular curves of full level are reduced.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_isReduced_residueField_tensorProduct_iff.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open IsLocalRing TensorProduct

theorem IsLocalRing.isReduced_residueField_tensorProduct_iff
    {A : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [Algebra A R] :
    IsReduced (ResidueField A ⊗[A] R) ↔ IsReduced (R ⧸ (maximalIdeal A).map (algebraMap A R)) := by sorry
